<!DOCTYPE html><html lang="en"><head>
  <meta charset="utf-8">
  <meta http-equiv="Content-Security-Policy" content="default-src 'none'; script-src 'self'; style-src 'self'; connect-src 'none'; img-src 'none'; font-src 'none'; object-src 'none'; base-uri 'none'; form-action 'none'; frame-src 'none'; worker-src 'none'">
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
  <title>S104 - Internal warm-up versus external paths</title>
  <link rel="stylesheet" href="styles.css">
  <script src="model.js" defer=""></script>
  <script src="app.js" defer=""></script>
</head>
<body>
  <main>
    <p class="training">Training rehearsal - synthetic data - not a live Azure result</p>
    <h1>S104: Internal success can hide external failure</h1>
    <p>A-S104 / D-S104 / SC-S104 - one frozen S lesson. Compare internal warm-up with the external host, redirect, callback, authentication and routing path.</p>
    <p><strong>DATA ONLY:</strong> All host names, redirects, state tokens, authentication and destinations are fixed teaching labels. No requests, real callbacks, registration, sign-in or configuration changes occur.</p>

    <section aria-labelledby="exercise-heading">
      <h2 id="exercise-heading">Record a bounded synthetic comparison</h2>
      <p>Precondition: the internal warm-up fixture always reports HTTP 200 in 32 synthetic ms. That alone proves none of the external path. A complete external journey must pass every check within 250 synthetic ms.</p>
      <form id="comparison-form">
        <label for="fixture">Teaching condition</label>
        <select id="fixture" name="fixture" required="">
          <option value="approved">Approved external path</option>
          <option value="host-mismatch">External host-header mismatch</option>
          <option value="redirect-loop">External redirect loop</option>
          <option value="callback-state-lost">External callback loses state</option>
          <option value="authentication-fails">External authentication fails</option>
          <option value="routing-mismatch">External destination differs</option>
          <option value="external-unobserved">External path unobserved</option>
          <option value="callback-unobserved">Callback observation missing</option>
        </select>
        <label for="operator-action">Operator action</label>
        <select id="operator-action" name="operator-action" required="">
          <option value="warm-up">Record internal warm-up only</option>
          <option value="compare">Compare with the external teaching trace</option>
        </select>
        <div class="buttons">
          <button id="record-comparison" type="submit">Record comparison</button>
          <button id="reset-lesson" type="button">Reset current exercise</button>
        </div>
      </form>
      <p id="input-error" role="alert" aria-live="assertive" tabindex="-1" hidden=""></p>
      <p>Keyboard: Tab between controls, arrow keys to choose, Enter to record. Reset restores defaults and focus, but retains all session history. Maximum 12 records; invalid selections never consume a record.</p>
    </section>

    <section id="comparison-result" data-status="failure" aria-labelledby="assessment" aria-live="polite">
      <h2 id="assessment">External assessment: failure</h2>
      <p id="eligibility">Not eligible. Internal health success cannot approve the external path.</p>
      <p id="explanation">Internal warm-up succeeded, but external failures were detected: authentication, journey.</p>
      <p id="internal-result">Internal warm-up: success; internal-host-label; warm-up-label; HTTP 200; 32 synthetic ms.</p>
      <p id="external-duration">External journey duration: 180 synthetic ms; budget 250 ms.</p>
      <div class="table-scroll">
        <table>
          <caption>Fixed external teaching trace - durations are synthetic, not a stopwatch or network measurement</caption>
          <thead><tr><th scope="col">Check</th><th scope="col">Result</th><th scope="col">Observed teaching data</th><th scope="col">Synthetic duration</th></tr></thead>
          <tbody id="external-trace"><tr data-check="host" data-status="success"><td>host</td><td>success</td><td>Expected production-host-label; observed production-host-label</td><td>12 synthetic ms</td></tr><tr data-check="redirect" data-status="success"><td>redirect</td><td>success</td><td>1 approved hop; no loop</td><td>30 synthetic ms</td></tr><tr data-check="callback" data-status="success"><td>callback</td><td>success</td><td>Expected lesson-state-A; observed lesson-state-A</td><td>40 synthetic ms</td></tr><tr data-check="authentication" data-status="failure"><td>authentication</td><td>failure</td><td>Teaching authentication failure</td><td>25 synthetic ms</td></tr><tr data-check="routing" data-status="success"><td>routing</td><td>success</td><td>Expected candidate-label; observed candidate-label</td><td>13 synthetic ms</td></tr><tr data-check="journey" data-status="failure"><td>journey</td><td>failure</td><td>HTTP 401; 180 synthetic ms; budget 250 ms</td><td>180 synthetic ms</td></tr></tbody>
        </table>
      </div>
      <p>Step durations describe individual fixture observations. The journey duration is the complete synthetic journey, not the sum of table rows. Missing measurements stay unknown, never zero.</p>
    </section>

    <section aria-labelledby="history-heading">
      <h2 id="history-heading">Retained page-session history</h2>
      <p id="counts" aria-live="polite">Attempts 6; success 1; failure 4; unknown 1; remaining 6.</p>
      <p id="history-note">6 of 12 session records retained. Reset preserves negative/unknown results and the allowance.</p>
      <ol id="history"><li data-sequence="1" data-status="unknown">Run 1: Approved external path; warm-up; internal success; external unknown; duration unknown; not eligible.</li><li data-sequence="2" data-status="failure">Run 2: External callback loses state; compare; internal success; external failure; 180 synthetic ms; not eligible.</li><li data-sequence="3" data-status="success">Run 3: Approved external path; compare; internal success; external success; 180 synthetic ms; synthetic eligible.</li><li data-sequence="4" data-status="failure">Run 4: External host-header mismatch; compare; internal success; external failure; 180 synthetic ms; not eligible.</li><li data-sequence="5" data-status="failure">Run 5: External redirect loop; compare; internal success; external failure; 240 synthetic ms; not eligible.</li><li data-sequence="6" data-status="failure">Run 6: External authentication fails; compare; internal success; external failure; 180 synthetic ms; not eligible.</li></ol>
    </section>

    <section aria-labelledby="limits-heading">
      <h2 id="limits-heading">What this lesson does not establish</h2>
      <p>Expected assertion: detect external failures despite internal health success; approved redirects do not loop or lose state. A missing external or callback observation is unknown, not eligible.</p>
      <p>No live Azure, external-host, callback, authentication, routing or source-parent certification. B-S104 is a separate native slice; D-S104 retains its P006 prerequisite and original acceptance gates. IaC: N/A.</p>
      <p>Portable standard HTML and JavaScript only. Node 22 is test tooling, not production Node 24 qualification. Existing offline Playwright 1.56.1 and signed Edge 156 bound the recorded browser observations; the lifecycle prototype remains unqualified.</p>
    </section>
  </main>


</body></html>